<article class="prose">
  <h1>LavaUI documentation</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    LavaUI is a declarative UI framework in Swift that draws with Vulkan. Views
    are written the way SwiftUI writes them; underneath, Yoga lays them out,
    HarfBuzz shapes the text and one pipeline draws everything, in a window of
    its own or as a client of the Lava compositor.
  </p>
  <p>
    New here? Start with <a href="/guide/getting-started">Getting started</a>,
    then the <a href="/guide/api">API guide</a>. The reference below is
    generated from the source's <code>///</code> comments.
  </p>
</article>

<section class="cards">
  {{#modules}}
  <a class="card" href="{{url}}">
    <h2>{{title}}</h2>
    {{#summary}}<p class="card-summary">{{summary}}</p>{{/summary}}
    <p>{{symbols}} declarations · {{documented}} documented</p>
  </a>
  {{/modules}}
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="section-title">Guides</h2>
  <ul class="link-list">
    {{#guides}}<li><a href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a></li>{{/guides}}
  </ul>
</section>
